  31:     Extend row bars periodically across the opposite side of a separator column.
  32: 
  33:     Input structure:
  34:     - bg = background. A near-solid vertical separator divides the grid into two sides.
  35:     - One side contains horizontal colored bars; the other side is blank target space.
  36:     - Bars may be stacked by row and may sit at different distances from the separator.
  37: 
  38:     Rule:
  39:     - Identify the separator as the column whose non-bg cells are one color.
  40:     - Treat the denser side as the bar side and collect each contiguous row run.
  41:     - Process bars from nearest to farthest from the separator; for each bar, paint its
  42:       color every bar-length cells into the blank side without overwriting earlier paint.
  43: 
  44:     Key insight: Each bar's length is the period for its extension, and nearer bars claim target cells first.
